        "section": [
          {
            "text": {
              "status": "generated",
              "div": "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">COPD exacerbation, treated with bronchodilators and steroids</div>"
            },
            "code": {
              "coding": [
                {
                  "code": "67781-5",
                  "system": "http://loinc.org",
                  "display": "Summarization of encounter note"
                }
              ]
            },
            "title": "Synthesis"
          },
          {
            "text": {
              "status": "generated",
              "div": "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">Dear colleague, I am writing to inform you about the recent admission of your 75-year-old female patient, who presented to our department with an acute exacerbation of her known chronic obstructive pulmonary disease. On admission, she exhibited increased dyspnoea, productive cough, and reduced oxygen saturation. Chest X-ray confirmed hyperinflation without evidence of pneumonia. Arterial blood gas analysis revealed hypoxaemia with mild hypercapnia. Blood tests showed elevated inflammatory markers. She was treated with inhaled bronchodilators via nebuliser, systemic corticosteroids, and supplemental oxygen therapy. Pulse oximetry was monitored continuously throughout her stay. She responded well to treatment with significant clinical improvement. Prior to discharge, patient education regarding inhaler technique and exacerbation management was provided. We recommend close outpatient follow-up and continuation of optimised inhaler therapy. Please do not hesitate to contact us should you have any questions.</div>"
            },
